+
+## Signed authority-store samples
+
+The separate policy/quota authority owner verifies signed time attestations
+against its durable issuer registry. Exported samples retain sealed issuer ID,
+epoch, public key and registry revision. Each consuming mutation revalidates
+that provenance in its own transaction before using the sample. A sample from
+an untrusted registry or a revoked/rotated issuer cannot advance authority time.
+
+The persisted numeric floor is a historical observation used by internal
+restart maintenance; it does not manufacture a public trusted-time capability.
+Issuer-provenance validation does not by itself establish wall-clock freshness.
+The configured time provider must still supply fresh authenticated observations;
+repeated identical valid attestations do not prove elapsed time.
